# ComputePH environment variables
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL — REQUIRED ON ALL VERCEL DEPLOYMENTS (Production,
# Preview, and Development) and the single control point for canonical
# URLs, Open Graph URLs, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, and JSON-LD.
#
# Format: an absolute http(s) URL, origin/root domain only (trailing slash
# optional; query strings, fragments, and sub-paths are rejected). The
# production value is the project's Vercel URL — do not deploy with a
# placeholder.
#
# Behavior:
#   - Vercel (any environment): the build FAILS with a clear error if this
#     is not set, or if the value is not an HTTPS URL.
#   - Local `npm run dev`: optional (defaults to http://localhost:3000).
#   - Local production builds: optional; falls back to the documented
#     default origin with a build-time warning.
#
# Production value:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://computeph.vercel.app
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID — OPTIONAL. Microsoft Clarity project ID from
# the Clarity dashboard (clarity.microsoft.com → Project → Settings → Overview).
# When unset or empty, the Clarity script is not loaded at all. When set, the
# script still loads only after the visitor allows analytics in the consent
# banner. NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the browser bundle at build time
# (a project ID is public by design, not a secret).
#
# Set it locally in .env.local and on Vercel (Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables, all environments), then redeploy so the build picks it up:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=your-clarity-project-id
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ComputePH Money Brief newsletter — Brevo (server-side only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create a contact list and a Double Opt-In (DOI) template in Brevo. The API
# key must stay server-side: never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit
# a real value.
#
# BREVO_API_KEY: Brevo → SMTP & API → API Keys.
# BREVO_LIST_ID: numeric ID of the list that confirmed subscribers join.
# BREVO_DOI_TEMPLATE_ID: numeric ID of the Brevo DOI confirmation template.
# BREVO_DOI_REDIRECT_URL: optional; defaults to NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL/#newsletter.
BREVO_API_KEY=
BREVO_LIST_ID=
BREVO_DOI_TEMPLATE_ID=
# BREVO_DOI_REDIRECT_URL=https://your-domain.com/#newsletter
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Community feedback — Web3Forms
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web3Forms access keys are public by design (they act as an email alias), but
# keep the value in .env.local / deployment settings rather than source code.
# Without a key the feedback form shows a safe configuration error and does not
# send anything.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=your-web3forms-access-key
